  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pre-departure Medical Services for Canada-bound refugees</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through this project, IOM&apos;s Migration Health Division will ensure that refugees accepted for resettlement to Canada by the Immigration, Refugees, and Citizenship Canada (IRCC) will receive pre-departure medical services such as immigration medical examinations, vaccinations, treatment of conditions of public health importance, pre-embarkation checks and medical assistance for movements. IOM will also provide outbreak management. The costs of the pre-departure medical services are covered by the Interim Federal Health Program (IFHP) based on a &#x201c;fee for service&#x201d; model though Medavie Blue Cross, a Canadian non-profit company, which administers funds for governmental and non-governmental agencies and serves as the claims administrator under contract with IRCC.</narrative>
  </description>
